    "explanation": "To both parties. This is an upfront-quoted RYDE_X trip (TRP-04005): Rider R-1846 booked Causeway Point to Ang Mo Kio Hub for a fixed fare of SGD 22.25 (EV-FARE-04005 quoted_fare_sgd 22.25; distance_charged_km 14.20; EV-TRIP-04005 booked optimal 14.20 km, 25 min). The GPS trace (EV-GPS-04005) records 20.57 km driven, an excess of 6.37 km or 44.86% over the booked route, which establishes a route deviation under POL-RD-01.\n\nThe deviation is the rider's own request. MSG-04005-003 (EV-CHAT-04005), sent by the rider at 15:59:50, asks the driver to stop at Northpoint first to collect a cake; the platform resolved that message's waypoint_hint to Northpoint City (1.4289, 103.8357), and the trace's nearest fix passes 55.0 m away, inside POL-RD-04's 200 m corroboration test. The rider does not dispute the request in her statement. POL-RD-04 therefore excludes the detour excess from any deviation charge against the driver.\n\nBecause the fare was fixed at booking, POL-RD-11 governs the rider's side: she is already whole on distance and time, POL-RD-02 does not run, and she owes nothing further. charged_total is 22.25, equal to the quote, so charged_over_quote is 0.00; there are no ERP, toll, airport-surcharge or waiting-time lines. The rider's payment state stands unchanged, and the driver's request for SGD 6.00 is not charged to her.\n\nWhat remains is the driver's compensation under POL-RD-04. He was billed for 14.20 km but drove 20.57 km, a shortfall of 6.37 km, above the 1.0 km trigger. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre: 6.37 x 0.75 = SGD 4.7775, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 4.80, within the SGD 15.00 cap. The SGD 6.00 originally claimed corresponds to no line of the fare breakdown and to no formula in the policy. Under POL-GEN-03 this is platform/fee-funded driver compensation (driver_compensation_sgd), not a charge on the rider, and on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling amount_sgd carries the same figure. The monetary effect (SGD 4.80) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and executes on issue.\n\nNo escalation applies. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07 (195 fixes at a 10 s cadence, no gaps, largest step 216.7 m, highest speed 78.0 km/h). Trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown. No exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact: EV-ADVIS-04005-01 (TRAFFIC_ADVISORY) is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0, but the driver asserts no external traffic cause and POL-RD-03 is not invoked, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is not capped below the 0.70 floor.\n\nOn the POL-RD-06 check: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 330 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and no conduct referral arises; the deviation is also not material (6.37 km is under 8.0 km and 44.86% is under 50%), and no billing-integrity referral arises because there is no unmatched charge line. The rider's point that the driver's filing narrative cites no evidence ID is noted but does not change the outcome: the driver's brief and the rider's own artifacts establish the facts, and no finding rests on the narrative alone."
